@@ -0,0 +1,131 @@
+# Mid-cycle plan changes
+
+## What and why
+
+Customers cannot change plan today: support cancels and resubscribes them by hand. This adds
+self-serve plan changes (upgrades, downgrades, and switching between monthly and annual billing),
+prorated so nobody pays twice for the same days and nobody is refunded for time already bought.
+See [ADR 0001](../docs/adr/0001-plan-change-proration-and-deferral.md) for the policy and why it was chosen.
+
+## Interface (fixed, verbatim)
+
+- `BillingService.change_plan(subscription_id: str, new_plan_code: str, new_interval: Interval | None = None) -> Invoice | None`
+  in `src/billing/service.py`. `new_interval=None` keeps the subscription's current interval.
+- Return the invoice issued for the change (recorded in the store like every other invoice),
+  or `None` when nothing is billed at the moment of the request.
+- Add `InvalidPlanChange(BillingError)` to `src/billing/errors.py` for change requests that
+  can't be honoured; keep using the existing error classes where they already fit.
+
+## Behaviour
+
+Terms (upgrade, downgrade, lateral change, scheduled change, remaining days) are defined in
+`GLOSSARY.md`. "Today" is `clock.today()`. The **target** of a request is
+`(new_plan_code, new_interval or subscription.interval)`. Every request states the full target.
+
+### Classification
+
+Compare the current plan and target plan by **monthly list price**, whatever interval the
+customer is on or moving to:
+
+- higher → upgrade, lower → downgrade
+- equal, different plan → lateral change
+- same plan → no plan change, but the interval may still change
+
+### Active subscription
+
+| Request | Now | At period end (next renewal) |
+|---|---|---|
+| Upgrade, same interval | Plan changes; invoice with credit and charge lines; any scheduled change discarded | Bills new plan, full price |
+| Upgrade + interval switch | Plan changes; invoice at **current-interval** prices; schedules `(new plan, new interval)` | New period of new interval, full price |
+| Downgrade (with or without interval switch) | Schedules the target; returns `None` | Moves to target, bills its full price |
+| Same plan, interval switch | Schedules the target; returns `None` | New period of new interval, full price |
+| Lateral (with or without interval switch) | Schedules the target; returns `None` | Moves to target, bills its full price |
+| Upgrade whose two rounded lines sum to 0.00 | Plan changes as for any upgrade; returns `None`, no invoice | As for upgrade |
+| Same plan and interval, change scheduled | Scheduled change cancelled; returns `None` | Renews as before |
+| Same plan and interval, nothing scheduled | `InvalidPlanChange` | n/a |
+
+Proration (upgrade invoice):
+
+- `period_days = period_end - period_start`, `remaining_days = period_end - today` (today inclusive,
+  period end exclusive), both in calendar days.
+- Credit line = `-(current plan price × remaining_days ÷ period_days)`.
+  Charge line = `new plan price × remaining_days ÷ period_days`. Both use the prices of the
+  subscription's **current** interval and are computed exactly.
+- Each line is rounded to cents, half up, on its own. The total is the sum of the two rounded lines.
+  The net is never rounded separately.
+- The credit is for the plan the subscription is on right now. A scheduled change has not happened yet.
+- The invoice is issued today, has exactly two lines (credit, then charge), and is recorded in the store.
+  `period_start`/`period_end` do not move.
+
+### Trialing subscription
+
+Any change (upgrade, downgrade, lateral, interval switch) applies immediately: plan and interval are
+replaced, `period_end` (trial end) does not move, nothing is scheduled, and no invoice is recorded.
+The method returns `None`. At trial end the customer is billed the full price of the plan and
+interval they are on by then.
+
+### Rejections
+
+All rejections leave the subscription and the store untouched: no invoice, no change to any
+scheduled change.
+
+- Canceled subscription → `SubscriptionNotActive`
+- Unknown subscription → `SubscriptionNotFound`; unknown plan → `PlanNotFound`
+- Overdue renewal (`period_end <= today`, `renew_due` not yet run) → `InvalidPlanChange`
+- Same plan and interval with nothing scheduled → `InvalidPlanChange`
+- Retired target plan → `PlanNotAvailable`. This covers an interval switch that keeps a retired plan.
+  A customer on a retired plan can move to any active plan. A request that only cancels a scheduled change
+  (target = current plan and interval) is allowed even if the current plan is retired.
+
+### Renewal
+
+`renew_due` applies a scheduled change at the first renewal after the request: the new period
+starts at the old `period_end`, uses the scheduled plan and interval, and bills that interval's
+full price. The scheduled change is then cleared. A scheduled target that is retired before the
+period ends is still applied, because it was sellable when the customer chose it.
+
+## Acceptance criteria (each is a test in `tests/test_plan_change.py`)
+
+Fixture plans: Basic 10/100, Pro 30/300, Premium 75/750 (monthly/annual).
+
+- [ ] Upgrade Basic→Pro monthly, period Jan 15–Feb 15, on Jan 25: invoice issued Jan 25, lines −6.77 / +20.32, total 13.55; period unchanged; Feb 15 renewal bills 30.00.
+- [ ] Per-line rounding: same setup on Feb 12: lines −0.97 / +2.90, total 1.93 (not 1.94).
+- [ ] Half-up: Basic→Plus (10.05/mo) on Apr 28 in an Apr 1–May 1 period: lines −1.00 / +1.01.
+- [ ] Change on the first day of the period: lines −10.00 / +30.00.
+- [ ] Annual upgrade Basic→Pro with `new_interval=None`, Jan 15 2026–Jan 15 2027, on Jul 15: annual prices, lines −50.41 / +151.23; stays annual.
+- [ ] Downgrade returns `None`, no invoice, plan unchanged until period end; renewal bills Basic 10.00.
+- [ ] Downgrade + switch to annual: `None`; renewal bills 100.00 for a 12-month period.
+- [ ] Monthly→annual on the same plan: `None`; renewal bills 300.00 for a 12-month period.
+- [ ] Annual→monthly on the same plan: `None`; nothing billed until Jan 15 2027, which bills 30.00 for one month.
+- [ ] Upgrade + switch to annual: invoice at monthly prices now (13.55); plan is Pro, still monthly; renewal bills 300.00 annual.
+- [ ] Upgrade while a downgrade is scheduled: on Pro (period Mar 1–Apr 1), Basic scheduled Mar 5, Premium requested Mar 11 → invoice total 30.49 (from Pro), scheduled change discarded; Apr 1 renewal bills 75.00.
+- [ ] Upgrade with no interval switch discards a scheduled interval switch.
+- [ ] A new request replaces the scheduled change.
+- [ ] Same plan and interval cancels a scheduled change and returns `None`; with nothing scheduled it raises `InvalidPlanChange`.
+- [ ] Lateral change (with interval switch) is scheduled, returns `None`, no invoice; renewal bills the new plan and interval.
+- [ ] An upgrade whose lines cancel out (Pro 30/300 → Studio 31/300 on annual) applies now and returns `None` with no invoice.
+- [ ] An upgrade + switch replaces a scheduled downgrade; a scheduled target retired before period end still applies; a customer on a retired plan can cancel their scheduled change.
+- [ ] Trial: downgrade + interval switch applies immediately, returns `None`, no invoice, trial end unchanged; trial end bills the new plan and interval at full price. A trial upgrade also returns `None`.
+- [ ] Rejections: canceled, unknown plan, retired target, retired current plan interval switch, overdue renewal, each leaving the subscription and invoices unchanged.
+- [ ] A customer on a retired plan can upgrade off it.
+- [ ] Missed renewals: a scheduled change applies to the first caught-up period and stays applied.
+
+## Open question
+
+Upgrades are classified by monthly price but prorated at the current interval's prices. A plan that
+is dearer monthly but cheaper annually (for example Pro 30/300 → X 31/250) therefore produces a
+negative-total upgrade invoice for an annual customer. The current plans don't have this shape, so this
+is left as specified and not tested. To be decided by the product owner.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+- Refunds and customer credit balances.
+- Changing a canceled subscription, or un-cancelling.
+- Changing plan prices, or prorating against historical prices (prices are immutable once stored).
+- Proration of trial time, and moving trial end.
+- Scheduling a change for an arbitrary future date.
+
+## Scope limits
+
+Touches `errors.py`, `money.py` (proration helper), `subscriptions.py` (scheduled change),
+`service.py` (`change_plan`, renewal), `__init__.py` exports, README, tests, glossary, ADR.
